course: dictionary
lesson: 13636
title: Inedible: not fit to eat
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Edible means safe and fit to eat. Inedible is the opposite: the prefix in- means "not", so inedible means not fit or safe to eat. Look for the clues around the word. «The mushrooms looked tasty, but they were inedible and poisonous.» The word poisonous tells you why they cannot be eaten.
explain: Inedible can mean more than one thing. Sometimes it means something is dangerous to eat, like poisonous wild berries. Sometimes it is just informal: «The burnt toast was inedible.» Here nobody is in danger. The toast simply tasted so bad that nobody could eat it.
explain: Things can also be inedible because they are not food at all. «Pebbles and bark are inedible, so leave them alone.» Use the word-swap check: put "not fit to eat" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. It does, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Inedible means not fit or safe to eat.
fact: The prefix in- means "not", so inedible is the opposite of edible.
fact: «Inedible» can mean poisonous, rotten, or not food at all.
fact: In an informal sense, «inedible» means tasting so bad that you cannot eat it, as with «the burnt toast».
fact: Many wild berries and mushrooms are inedible or poisonous, so never eat wild plants without an expert adult.
exercise: «The mushrooms looked tasty, but they were inedible.» What does inedible mean? | *Not safe to eat, because it is poisonous | Very large and round | Sweet and sticky | Cooked and ready to serve
exercise: «The burnt toast was so bad that Dad said it was inedible.» What does inedible mean here? | Very soft and warm | Cut into four neat pieces | *Tasting so bad you cannot eat it | Covered in jam
exercise: Which of these is inedible? | A ripe banana | A boiled egg | *A pebble from the beach | A slice of bread
test: Which word means the same as not fit to eat? | fresh | *inedible | tasty | edible
test: «Some wild berries are inedible, so do not pick and eat them.» Why should you not eat them? | They are the wrong colour | They are too big to fit in your mouth | *They might be poisonous | They are too cold
exam: Sam finds berries in the woods and wants to eat them. What should he do first? | Share them with his friends without checking | Pick the biggest ones and put them in his pocket | *Ask an expert adult, because some wild berries are inedible or poisonous | Eat one to see if it tastes nice
